course: dictionary
lesson: 12569
title: Diligent: working hard and with care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diligent means working hard and taking great care. A diligent person does not rush. They pay attention to the details and keep going when the task is tricky.
explain: Look at the words around it: «Maya was diligent, and she checked every sum twice before handing in her work.» Checking twice shows she takes care, so diligent must be a good thing to be.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence: «Maya was hard-working and careful, and she checked every sum twice» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: «Diligent» means working hard and carefully, and paying attention to details.
fact: «Diligent» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «a diligent pupil» or «a diligent worker».
fact: «A diligent search» means a search done carefully and thoroughly, leaving nothing out.
fact: «Due diligence» is a formal phrase meaning careful checking before a decision is made.
fact: Diligent is close in meaning to hard-working, but it adds care and attention to detail.
exercise: «Maya was a diligent student who checked every answer twice.» What does diligent mean? | Lazy and careless | *Working hard and carefully | Loud and noisy | Very tired after a long day
exercise: Ben wants to be a diligent worker. What is a diligent worker like? | Careless and quick to stop | Happy to sleep at lunch | *Careful and hard-working | Always late for work
exercise: «The police made a diligent search of the park.» What does diligent suggest about the search? | It was done by a dog only | *It was done carefully and thoroughly | It was done quickly, with no care | It was a short, rude search
test: Which word is closest in meaning to diligent? | Lazy | Careless | *Hard-working | Silly
test: «Sara's diligent study helped her pass the test.» What does diligent study mean? | Study that lasted only one minute | Study done quickly while watching TV | Study that nobody could see | *Study done with hard work and care
exam: Which sentence uses diligent correctly? | The diligent sandwich was very tasty | The diligent cat slept all day | The diligent storm knocked down the tree | *The diligent pupil checked her spelling carefully
